HBUILD - Assigned world-building ranges

Everyone: hbuild mine
Staff (including implementors) and assigned builders: hbuild info
Owners manage assignments for existing saved characters:
  hbuild assign <name> <start> [count]  Default 50 rooms; count 1-500.
  hbuild unassign <name>               Remove ALL of that builder's ranges.
  hbuild ranges                        Show everyone's assignments.

Example: hbuild assign Aria 8000 assigns rooms 8000-8049 inclusive.
Ranges may not overlap. IDs must stay within 2-8999. Assignment does not
create, erase or overwrite any rooms. Owners can edit any existing room.
All other builders, including admins, edit only their assigned ranges.

Builder commands:
  hbuild create <room>                 Create an unused assigned room.
  hbuild name <text>                   Rename the current room (1-79 chars).
  hbuild describe <text>               Replace its long description (1-180 chars).
  hbuild link <direction> <room>       Add a one-way exit within your ranges.
  hbuild unlink <direction>            Remove a current-room exit.

Changes save immediately in the original world format. Existing rooms cannot
be overwritten by create. Existing exits must be unlinked before replacement.
Directions: north, south, east, west, northeast, northwest, southeast,
southwest, up, down. Use full lowercase directions. A return exit must be
created separately from the other room. Keep text printable ASCII.

Use hdm goto <room> to enter an existing assigned room. Ask an owner to
connect your area to the public world; both ends of a builder's link must be
assigned. New rooms are empty; existing flags and permanent contents remain.
Assignments persist and confer no moderation or class powers. Use hbuild
unassign to remove range access; hstaff revoke removes the role separately.
Unassigning retains completed rooms. Corrupt data denies building access.
The audit records authorized buildtry/rangetry attempts before effects;
read the command response to confirm success. Class and level stay intact.
